 "notes": "The machine on an 8-tick beat. Per cycle: the carrier is pulled out of the quasi cell (power away, A never updated, keeps its head); 3 ticks later BOTH pistons push, so in ONE block-entity phase U's stone lands beside A first (its update reaches A while the power is away: retract queued AFTER that tick's block events, so it is still pending in the next player window = ARMED) and the carrier lands right behind it (power back, so the pending event is a no-op at the next block-event phase and A keeps its head); two ticks later U pulls its stone back while the power is on (that update is harmless), then the carrier is pulled again. Never retract U while its stone is still moving: the spit finalises the stone in the block-event phase and that update, with the power away, retracts A. A is placed by the build and woken by one block placed and broken beside it (a survival player simply places A last, when the carrier is in the quasi cell: its own placement check extends it).",
